<p>The United States has accused China of “massively” expanding its nuclear arsenal as Washington pushes to include Beijing in any future arms-control agreement after New START ended this month. US officials said New START’s end creates a chance to negotiate a follow-on deal that goes beyond the traditional US-Russia framework. China dismissed the US claims as unfounded and said Washington was “smearing” its nuclear policy.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/9dlsuY2SNbCAxuhQPHWe4q9uJEGdOabf8OPNTPwIkehKHmhEL8V1_Vfah7OVO7ZBUsXkLEREV1Z-YAxKSdIl-fE20Wm49YuZjMEUyWT12cfZmXeK_zN7DLY7_rkAyzZxHCPIPbBF3SNxTJc-mC05ojAPopmT8JdbZ-4LPvudwKo0lIbUQDVs8mE5Zv7Uv3H2_AJtkxcQkkbtEhNoGNEQlCYoWmIJsPK-sJSn_p2fqIbnqnRA73Y' alt='A member of the People’s Liberation Army during a military parade in Beijing, September 3, 2025.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Parity timeline: US officials said China could reach nuclear “parity” in four to five years, a claim China disputes.</li><li>Secret tests claim: The US renewed its allegation that China has carried out secret nuclear tests, tying the charge to its push for Beijing to join future treaties.</li><li>Arms race fears: Some coverage cast the dispute as fueling arms-race worries after New START’s expiration, even as China says it will not join such a race.</li><li>Treaty framing: US messaging stressed that any next agreement should include Beijing, signaling a push for broader participation than past US-Russia limits.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>US State Department: US officials said China is dramatically expanding its nuclear arsenal and repeated claims of secret nuclear tests, while urging that China be included in any future arms-control treaty. (<a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/united-states-canada/article/3344385/china-has-massively-expanded-its-nuclear-arsenal-claims-us-state-department'>South China Morning Post</a>)</li><li>Chinese government: China called the US allegations “groundless accusations” and said Washington was “smearing” its nuclear policy. (<a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2026/02/24/us-accuses-china-of-increasing-its-nuclear-arsenal_6750810_4.html'>Le Monde</a>)</li><li>Chinese government: China said it would not “engage in any nuclear arms race,” responding to US claims about the growth of its arsenal. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/feb/24/us-accuses-china-of-massively-expanding-nuclear-arsenal-amid-fears-of-new-arms-race'>The Guardian</a>)</li><li>US government: US officials said they have also spoken with other nuclear-armed allies, including Britain and France, as part of their arms-control outreach. (<a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/united-states/us-meeting-russian-and-chinese-delegations-for-nuclear-arms-control-talks-official-says'>The Straits Times</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/us-accuses-china-of-massively-expanding-nuclear-arsenal-11126130#publisher=newsstand'>US Accuses China Of &quot;Massively Expanding&quot; Nuclear Arsenal</a> - ndtv.com</li><li><a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2026/02/24/us-accuses-china-of-increasing-its-nuclear-arsenal_6750810_4.html'>US accuses China of increasing its nuclear arsenal</a> - lemonde.fr</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/us-says-china-massively-expanded-nuclear-arsenal/article70668686.ece'>U.S. says China &#x27;massively expanded&#x27; nuclear arsenal</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.firstpost.com/world/us-accuses-china-of-rapidly-expanding-nuclear-arsenal-calls-for-inclusion-in-future-arms-treaty-13982889.html'>US accuses China of rapidly expanding nuclear arsenal, calls for inclusion in future arms treaty</a> - firstpost.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/united-states/us-meeting-russian-and-chinese-delegations-for-nuclear-arms-control-talks-official-says'>US says China ‘massively expanded’ nuclear arsenal</a> - straitstime